Package: python3-ghee
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, python3-numpy, python3-pil
Recommends: python3-spidev, python3-libgpiod, python3-smbus2
Suggests: ffmpeg
Description: multi-pass GLSL renderer for small Linux devices
 ghee compiles a set of fragment shaders (a scene), renders them
 off-screen with GLES2 through DRM/GBM, and writes the pixels to image
 files, SPI panels, an HDMI display, or an H264 or MJPEG stream. No
 window system required.
 .
 Ships the ghee CLI and a browser-based live shader console.
 .
 python3-spidev, python3-libgpiod and python3-smbus2 drive the bundled SPI
 and I2C panel drivers. They are recommended, so apt installs them unless
 you say otherwise; everything else works without them.
 .
 ffmpeg is only needed on boards without the Broadcom H264 encoder (Pi 5
 and desktop), where the software encoder shells out to it. It is not
 pulled in; install it with apt install ffmpeg.
